{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder","id":342038,"title":"Masquerade Ball Murder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-16T09:58:47-08:00","id":342038,"title":"Masquerade Ball Murder","content":"I make a start in mine episodic <b>CtL</b> chronicle for our RPG club in two days with game session about escape of PCs on Christmas from their common Keeper in small town in New England. Today I got idea for our next session - the PCs and new players will be asked in time of carnival to come and join Masquerade Ball in old, deserted mansion by mysterious invitations. They will not know at first their host, only that they need to worn mask attached to massage - and masks are reinforcing their Masks so even they only see their &quot;human guise&quot;.<br /> <br /> Players will have time to socialize and forge the Courts in starting freehold. I even considering running mini LARP for this. And, of course, there will be murder on the ball. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have some questions with that you could help me...<br /> <br /> 1. What being could be the host? True Fae, hobgoblin, changeling, other? Come to think about it, maybe interesting would be Charlatan Fae?<br /> <br /> 2. I need many NPCs to make a PC group party in to ball - who could make for extras on the ball? Could mortals be compelled to join part for one night and not remembering it after? Because having about 50 of Lost in the town of about 2500 population I do not see on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:09:21-08:00","id":342061,"title":"","content":"If I was a Changeling, I wouldn't even attend something this suspicious. It screams &quot;faerie plot&quot;. Give them <i>reasons</i> to want to go to this thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:16:28-08:00","id":342067,"title":"","content":"Agree with the above poster. To mollify it, and to answer #1, maybe make the host a very well-trusted local Lost who's secretly a Loyalist/Privateer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:32:54-08:00","id":342107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342067#post342067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with the above poster. To mollify it, and to answer #1, maybe make the host a very well-trusted local Lost who's secretly a Loyalist/Privateer?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not any freehold, yet. All the changelings in area are PCs. It's very small and personal setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:50:04-08:00","id":342113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342107#post342107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is not any freehold, yet. All the changelings in area are PCs. It's very small and personal setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Well, I got nothing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:11:23-08:00","id":342131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342107#post342107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is not any freehold, yet. All the changelings in area are PCs. It's very small and personal setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have around <i>fifty</i> player characters? What the hell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:40:12-08:00","id":342146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342131#post342131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have around <i>fifty</i> player characters? What the hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I said there are few PCs ( probably around 5 ). A 50 are extras - best would be Mortals that are under spell for one night, and forget later about any of those events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:52:31-08:00","id":342149,"title":"","content":"I thought you had said there were 50 Changelings in the town, my misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> Regardless. Filling the ball with manipulated mortals is fine and all, but you need to have some sort of motivation for your player characters to attend this. If there's just a random ball reeking of faerie business and they're such a small group that doesn't even have a Freehold to turn to, it would be ridiculous for them to go along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T15:31:44-08:00","id":375621,"title":"","content":"i just assume they go - it's players job to make his character convinced to join the plot. Also, changelings had few weeks on their own, I bet they are a bit lonely and curious with all the thing. They also are fresh Lost, so are not as much paranoid for True Fae, yet. They really, for all the matter to this day, can get invitations from the other changeling for party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Host of the party is Banished True Fae, that was sent to Earth after he refused to take part in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion?p=373619#post373619\">The Game of local Feud of Gentry</a>. He now wants to destroy his once rivals and by spoiling <i>The Game</i> he hopes he will return to his once Arcadian domain. Inviting changelings is the way for him to make it easier.<br /> <br /> I have first scetch of plot. Let me know what do you think about it...<br /> <br /> 1. Arival of various changelings. Description of mansion - will use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350927-let-s-make-a-haunted-estate\">Hunted Estate mini-setting</a> here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 2. Ball room - beautifully decorated, like taken back from Victorian era when she was built. Guests are clothed with style, on Victorian style, mixed with some renesanse Italy elements, like Venetian masks. Every one are covered in Venetian masks, like those that PCs got in mysteroius package.<br /> 3. Host is also in mask - he greets the guests, ask for having fun and invite to dances. I'm not sure if the ball should be served by hobs, or maybe host is so much powerfull, his only wishes come to reality?<br /> 4. Let PCs to have time for interactions - maybe half an hour to one hour. Recall them their dreams and memories about Courts. <br /> 5. Second announcement of the Host - he will kill ech hour next mortal untill changelings will help him ( in fighting the True Fae ) or at least to stop it. Is it this too cheesy solution?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T17:38:33-08:00","id":376756,"title":"","content":"Wyrd,<br /> There's a bit of a fallacy there. It's everyone's job to build a good story together - and if the players don't want to be there, they'll sure as hell get up, walk out, and spend a session and a half bartering with Hobs in the local Goblin Market for a fixer-upper Hollow down the block from the local Hooters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T19:55:18-08:00","id":376868,"title":"","content":"I know, 'cuz I've known players who did just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T00:17:16-08:00","id":377024,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I think it can't be emphasized enough that everybody needs to work together. If players try to write themselves out of game that's bad but the ST needs to consider the motivations of the characters and not just shove them around like chess pieces.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">True Fae should be used sparingly or they lose their impact and changeling have good reason to be wary of any fae creature the could be linked to the Gentry. As such, if I could suggest, there\u2019s no reason Changelings can\u2019t run into a fine ghost story.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>The Backstory</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">50 years ago there was a masquerade ball at the old mansion but fire broke out and many of the guests were killed. The family fixed the place up but it never really felt the same and they moved out the following summer letting the old grounds rot.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Several (13? 25?) years later, on the anniversary of the ball invitations were received by the surviving members of the ball and their kin. Those who chose to attend found the ballroom was set for a party and there were already a number of guests milling and dancing to music. The hosts were not easy to identify beneath their masks but those who did catch a glimpse beneath their costumes could swear they were those same souls lost so many years ago in this very house. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">When morning came most of the guests had no memory of the nights entertainment while others were found dead in the old manner. Suspicion fell on many of the guests who had attended the phantom ball but no case held against any of them and ultimately the police had to accept that they simply did not know who the killer was.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Now the invitations have been received again. The ghosts of the masquerade seek to expand their number again.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>The PCs</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">If one or more PC\u2019s are willing they might be decedents of the survivors, or even survivors themselves. Heck, a changeling that only felt Arcadia as a short time might think the invitation is from the original family, their old friends!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Autumn courtiers may be curious and wish to study the ball while Summer changelings might attend with the goal of protecting the mortals.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Or maybe the PC\u2019s don\u2019t know anything about the old house and just get invitations in the mail inviting them to a party with promises of free food and drink. In this case the invitations should imply that the event is some kind of public party, such as a charity auction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>The Truth</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The phantom ball is hosted by the ghosts of those killed in the original fire, as well as the other souls they\u2019ve gathered along the way. Their magics wipe the memories of mortals afterwords, making the whole affair feel as nothing more than a dream. Supernaturals, including changelings, are immune to the memory editing effects.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The important question is why the ghosts are hosting this dance?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The ghosts might simply be lonely and pool their power to reunite with the living and gather fresh blood. Perhaps the original fire was a sacrifice to some powerful death god or spirit and now the ghosts are trying to gather other souls to buy their own freedom from this dark entity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Maybe the ghosts have no control over the dance. It could be a naturally occurring intersection of the living world and the great below. Murders follow because it\u2019s generally not a good idea to mix the living and the dead - there is just too much jealousy from the later towards the former. Alternatively the ghosts don\u2019t kill anyone. Instead another supernatural has realized these parties happen every so often and wipe the mortal minds making it the ideal place to kill off human rivals without any risk of witnesses remembering.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T00:21:01-08:00","id":377028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=376756#post376756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd,<br /> There's a bit of a fallacy there. It's everyone's job to build a good story together - and if the players don't want to be there, they'll sure as hell get up, walk out, and spend a session and a half bartering with Hobs in the local Goblin Market for a fixer-upper Hollow down the block from the local Hooters.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they do not want to be part of masquared, they can just skip the session. As I mentioned before - it's episodic campaign, with various players across the game sessions from our RPG club, with only one light general plot binding the game. They do not like this premise, then they can just do not attend this game, and come couple a weeks on next one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T03:06:22-08:00","id":377076,"title":"","content":"I am running a Masquerade ball in the next few sessions of my game, and have run the hell out of Castle Falkenstein, so I ahve some insights.<br /> <br /> One question is...what do they get out of it? What are their goals as PCs? In my case, for most it is Build approval with Courts (Mantle, Court Affinity), for some it is to publicly display their affection toward their paramour by publicly doing a minor ritual of putting some ivy in their hair, The Spring Queen is choosing a new paramour, and some PCs plan to...affect those proceedings based on who they would prefer she wind up with (none are making the play themselves as far as I know, but it was an option). Some are helping a clandestine meeting of the Autumn and Night (Moon) Court and covering up the meeting. Some fear an attacker who has caused chaos before may again so seek to guard the ball from it. And others just want to get people talking about their outfits/dancing and/or score with lovely men/women/both. Pretty much everyone has at least a couple things they want out of the ball. Your players should too. Note this is not to get them to show up...assumedly they have already shown interest. This is to give them stuff they enjoy.<br /> <br /> What do you plan to have occur? Depending you may want to talk to your players about some of it. Certainly, if you EXPECT the PCs to do something, you should discuss it with the players. Now I haven't as my ball will be very sandboxy...the PCs can make of it what they will. But depending on your intentions it can be good to discuss.<br /> <br /> What do the PLAYERS want from the ball? Ask em! They want romance? A chance to begin relationships? what are they after. Having a bunch of mortals who will forget it all would...limit my own interest, because whats the point of being social/beautiful/awesome if people forget? Of course, the intentions of whoever I play might affect that. Knowing what they think would be cool may be important to what they will enjoy. Some players will be disappointed if there is not combat. Others will be disappointed if there is combat. You can't please everyone, but you can know their interest.<br /> <br /> This kind of thing I have seen really be awesome and I have seen be the GM talking mostly to himself for a couple hours. Player investment is a major factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T05:28:23-08:00","id":377125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377024#post377024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I think it can't be emphasized enough that everybody needs to work together. If players try to write themselves out of game that's bad but the ST needs to consider the motivations of the characters and not just shove them around like chess pieces.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">True Fae should be used sparingly or they lose their impact and changeling have good reason to be wary of any fae creature the could be linked to the Gentry.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I want to incorporate PCs motivations, only players still do not want to send me them. But I think that curiosity is enough for young changelings to try to see what is it in there...<br /> <br /> As to usage of True Fae - I would agree that normally they should be used sparesly, but the clue of whole chronicle is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/373394-losts-population-explosion?p=373619#post373619\">sudden creation and fall of Freehold, because of local Feud's The Game competition</a>. Gentry want to to test changelings more instantly, and open the Arcadia more wide than in typical <b>CtL</b> setting. On first game session Arcadian Huntsman stole 5 mortals to his realm, on second players were maneuvering between Krampus hunt on mortal, and thier once Keeper hunt for them and mortal. It's just more &quot;direct&quot; setting than corebook one.<br /> <br /> As such, I think that idea about Banished Old God that want to get back on on rest of Feud by giving the local Lost clues about the Game itself - is totally in order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377024#post377024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">As such, if I could suggest, there\u2019s no reason Changelings can\u2019t run into a fine ghost story. &lt;Awesomeness&gt;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Really awesome one shot idea I would gladly use. Only not in this particular game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-21-2015, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T07:14:54-08:00","id":377211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377125#post377125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I want to incorporate PCs motivations, only players still do not want to send me them. But I think that curiosity is enough for young changelings to try to see what is it in there...</div> </div> </div> </div>It really shouldn't be, with what Changelings in general have gone through. I don't think it's a good enough motivation unless they're taking it upon themselves to investigate everything related to the Fae in the area or are planning to protect everyone from possibly supernatural influence. Or they're <i>heavily </i>Summer Court leaning with no sense of self-preservation. Quoting myself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342061#post342061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was a Changeling, I wouldn't even attend something this suspicious. It screams &quot;faerie plot&quot;. Give them <i>reasons</i> to want to go to this thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=342149#post342149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to have some sort of motivation for your player characters to attend this. If there's just a random ball reeking of faerie business and they're such a small group that doesn't even have a Freehold to turn to, it would be ridiculous for them to go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It don't think it's good form to plan something like this without considering the interests of the players and their characters, especially if you're just planning to leave them hanging in the case they can't find a good justification to pursue this story thread. There's always a certain degree of contrivance involved when you plan events in the game together with the players, but I entirely agree with BaronSamedi's points and HobbitGuy's observation. You really should involve your players and take into account their expectations, even if you can't satisfy everyone; because if you build railroads that only lead towards a certain direction and your players aren't interested in the destination or find the train fee unsatisfactory so to speak, most of your work ends up being wasted and no one's happy because there aren't alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-21-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T09:24:07-08:00","id":377270,"title":"","content":"I cannot run a Masquared Ball game session and run other location - players should know they PCs will need to be interested in play to work with that. If player is not interested in that larger gathering, he should not come to game session about it, don't he? I want to interwoven <i>PCs</i> motivations in to game, but still I need <i>players</i> to get me basic info what would interested they characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T09:34:06-08:00","id":377278,"title":"","content":"Do your players seriously refuse to offer input helpful for the building of the game even after you ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:21:15-08:00","id":377344,"title":"","content":"They just do not write back on my request for this. But I suspect they are just swept by work/school/life. They will probably write responses in few days. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For now, let's focus on plot idea itself - as I wrote earlier, I need to make some assumptions to go with session, if it is for less restrictive in terms of attendency game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:24:02-08:00","id":377345,"title":"","content":"I would recommend to wait with planning until you receive their feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T11:04:44-08:00","id":377378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377125#post377125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">As such, I think that idea about Banished Old God that want to get back on on rest of Feud by giving the local Lost clues about the Game itself - is totally in order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">In that case I have something I ran near the end of my last Changeling chronicle that you might mine for ideas.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Our story starts with a Gentry known as The Scarecrow King. 200 years ago he was a powerful and power hungry Autumn king. He did many terrible things to obtain strength in magic, in the freehold, and even in the mortal world but he justified himself to himself with the thought that all this personal power was for the greater good as it let him protect others. It was this lie that let him sleep at night.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">When his freehold wound up besieged by one of the Others the Scarecrow King managed to best the Fae and take a Title. In doing so he destroyed his freehold and ascended to become one of the Fair Folk himself. Still, he held tight to his lie - \u201cThis is all to help others.\u201d For the sake of this lie even as a True Fae he helps the Lost in his way. He plays games with freeholds arranging for them to win boons if they are strong enough and in exchange he gets the conflict, the story, he needs to survive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">In the present day The Scarecrow King challenged the PC\u2019s to a game. He would take 13 mortals connected to the freehold, friends, lovers, even children, and place both them and their fetches in the manner in the woods on All Hallows Eve. If the changelings could keep the majority of mortals safe until dawn then each freehold monarch would get the truthful answer to one question and all the mortals would be returned safely. If the majority of the mortals succumb to the dangers of the house then all the mortals would be forfeit and the changelings would get only the fetches as consolation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The house was decorated as a Halloween party and everyone that entered (including a local Werewolf pack) was magically costumed so they could not be recognized. Nobody could recognize one another nor the mortals and fetches nor the phantasmal monsters of the house on sight nor scent. The first challenge was simply telling who was who. Luckily the changelings had prepared by knowing one another\u2019s desires, fears, and sorrows as well as those of their mortals.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">All the side rooms of the mansion have various puzzles and challenges where they could free this mortal/fetch or with threats that might \u201ckill\u201d* the guests if they weren\u2019t stopped. These ranged from riddles to Professor Layton puzzles to combat. In addition to the mitigation of threat solving puzzles also rewarded the changelings with various objects* including 2 keys. The artifacts didn\u2019t do much in the way of magic but tended to be helpful elsewhere. A thesaurus that always opens to the last word spoken isn\u2019t that great unless you need help solving a riddle before the timer runs out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">As morning approached I threw one last curveball - the house started collapsing. Anyone trapped inside would be \u201ckilled.\u201d In the last few minutes (and this was being run in real time!) the PC\u2019s realized that they needed a key to get out of the locked house. There was no front door nor any other exit so they just needed to be touching the key. They looked at their two keys and realized one has a sun printed on it and the other was labeled \u201cThere\u2019s no place like home.\u201d After a quick argument they arrived at the correct conclusion. They needed the key to survive dawn not a key to get home.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">At this point they had 10 or 11 mortals left and nobody could quite decide which of these were real humans and which were fetches. They ran the clock down to 20 seconds arguing about which mortals they could take with them before the Sumer King remembers they only needed to save 7+ mortals, saving fetches had no penalty. Again, this was run in real time. I was sitting there with a timer watching them. It was pretty amazing and was some awesome catharsis as I announced the house melting back into forest and all 13 friends and family safely around them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">* The whole manner was a dream so deaths were not permanent, everyone would be fine in the morning so long as the PC\u2019s won and got the mortals back. Going to Arcadia isn\u2019t a great option even if your new keeper is \u201csympathetic.\u201d All the bric-a-brac of the house and, indeed, the house itself was also phantasmal and vanished in dawns first rays.<br /> <br /> This all probably isn't exactly what you want to do but I hope it can provide some ideas for your masquerade XD</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T11:13:10-08:00","id":377387,"title":"","content":"Okay, here are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> The core problem you're trying to tackle here is &quot;How do I get my players interested in the main plot line?&quot; This is a very common challenge, especially in modern horror settings.<br /> <br /> The issue is that you're trying to force this interest (via a villain/employer hybrid) in the course of one session. Believe me, from experience: it often takes multiple sessions to get a motley to realise 'Huh, maybe we should look into this?' Drip feed the clues into what the players want to do, rather than force feeding them. The satisfaction they get from facing a challenge they uncovered themselves will be greater than if they're told 'Here's your main quest: complete it or else.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's look at the possible options your players may take when faced with an exiled Fae that's strong-arming them into doing what it wants:<br /> <br /> 1) They run away. These are fresh out of the hedge changelings with no backup: no Courts, no Freehold, no powerful contacts. They've been manipulated into a trap. If I was an Ogre in that situation, I'd make a door through the nearest wall. If I was Fairest, I'd blast Vainglory to buy enough time for everyone else to escape. The threat of killing hostages works only if the players care about mortal deaths: plenty of players are calous enough to let them die to save their own skin. Never assume heroic intentions in a World of Darkness game.<br /> <br /> 2) They attack the host. This is the reverse of running away: they take the heroic incentive to the logical conclusion. This is a villain, it's threatening to kill everyone... Combat time. If this is an exiled Fae, it should be diminished enough in power that a lucky or clever motley has a chance of hurting it. If it dies or runs away, you can take it from there easily: the players have saved the day and can take their own course of action in working out what's going on.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, they die. Or are captured. Nothing that incentivises them to suddenly start working for the thing, anyway.<br /> <br /> 3) They plain refuse to accept the terms, standing there doing nothing. See above concerning calous players. The Fae butchers a room full of mortals then probably attacks the motley. Then you're up at 2).<br /> <br /> 4) They go along with your plan. This actually the riskiest and most damaging course of action from a Changeling perspective. What the above posters are saying about overexposure of Gentry is true for multiple reasons. Just spending time with a True Fae long enough to have a conversation is a major Clarity breaking point. This alone should dissuade your players from sticking around to chat. Nowhere in any of the books (from what I remember) does it say anything about Exiled or Charlatan Fae being exempt from this effect.<br /> <br /> If the group then decides to start taking orders from the thing, regardless of the motivations, every other changeling that discovers this will consider them Loyalists. The fact that it's to save some lives will be irrelevant: many Loyalists work for their masters with similar threats or incentives looming over them. &quot;Bring me pretty things or your family spends a season on the Hurting-Go-Round...&quot;<br /> <br /> From your players perspective, they will resent the task given to them. Rather than curiosity pushing them to solve the case, they will try to solve the problem of &quot;How do we escape this servitude we've been forced into?&quot; They'll keep looking for the opportunity to enact any of the other options above, probably after freeing the hostages.<br /> <br /> Okay, all of the above is hypothetical. I hope it demonstrates all the directions a group of players can go, assuming they even accept the invitation and go to the party.<br /> <br /> Absolutely, plan a masquerade ball if that's what you want to do. Myself, I'd make the host an Ensorcelled mortal who moved to the area from another Freehold. He/she can use the opportunity to introduce the players to standard Freehold concepts: if the group has truly never meet any othe changelings outside of Arcadia, these are things they'll need to learn: the role of Courts, leadership, the threats that face the Lost and how to survive amongst regular people without turning into monsters.<br /> <br /> And, yes, plant a seed for a greater plot. Have a murder but keep it a mystery. Have a bloody, exhausted Changeling drop through a bathroom mirror, having just escaped Faerie. Don't stick a fully grown tree in front of the players and say &quot;This what you're going to climb.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T00:53:58-08:00","id":380850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core problem you're trying to tackle here is &quot;How do I get my players interested in the main plot line?&quot; This is a very common challenge, especially in modern horror settings.<br /> <br /> The issue is that you're trying to force this interest (via a villain/employer hybrid) in the course of one session. Believe me, from experience: it often takes multiple sessions to get a motley to realise 'Huh, maybe we should look into this?' Drip feed the clues into what the players want to do, rather than force feeding them. The satisfaction they get from facing a challenge they uncovered themselves will be greater than if they're told 'Here's your main quest: complete it or else.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned it before - it's episodic game, with various players changing a rooster on each game session. It is made once a couple a weeks. I <b>do not have time</b> to make it personal for them. This is why it's players responsibility to engage in story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) They run away. These are fresh out of the hedge changelings with no backup: no Courts, no Freehold, no powerful contacts. They've been manipulated into a trap. If I was an Ogre in that situation, I'd make a door through the nearest wall. If I was Fairest, I'd blast Vainglory to buy enough time for everyone else to escape. The threat of killing hostages works only if the players care about mortal deaths: plenty of players are calous enough to let them die to save their own skin. Never assume heroic intentions in a World of Darkness game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. But I would hope for at least intense debate within players group discussing to leave or try to rescue mortals. Also, I imagine if they would not comply, Exiled would kill the rest of mortals and some days later would found and visit each of PCs to &quot;change his mind&quot;. Some of them would end Loyalists. Rest would fight or be dead. Not a nice solution to the problem I could hint on players. He found them once ( to send message ), he can twice. Still, it's interesting scenario that ends quickly my ball scene, but changes in to &quot;Exiled hunts for changelings&quot; session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) They attack the host. This is the reverse of running away: they take the heroic incentive to the logical conclusion. This is a villain, it's threatening to kill everyone... Combat time. If this is an exiled Fae, it should be diminished enough in power that a lucky or clever motley has a chance of hurting it. If it dies or runs away, you can take it from there easily: the players have saved the day and can take their own course of action in working out what's going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, PCs saves the day. Only they killed they, at least for now, only source for information The Game of Gentry in making. Still, I think this heroic ending is also suitable to <b>Changeling</b> game - it's a story about survivors, is not this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, they die. Or are captured. Nothing that incentivises them to suddenly start working for the thing, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally do not kill PCs, but in this lighten game format I think it's totally okay. In confrontation with True Fae some Lost will be lost forever - and it's suitable to convention. And as it's lighter game, I players can return with new character next time, this that &quot;run away&quot; from next Keeper, as part of The Game. Also, we have martyr that was killed by Fae - I think most of other changelings will then work more eagerly to creat Freehold and Courts for protection from this happening again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) They plain refuse to accept the terms, standing there doing nothing. See above concerning calous players. The Fae butchers a room full of mortals then probably attacks the motley. Then you're up at 2).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the blood they have on their hands. I imagine their dreams filled with imagery of those murders repeating each night from the fateful night. I even could make a Nightmare Condition for this. Also, interesting could be that Gentry taking part in The Game, would use those dreams for very nefarious purpose. Maybe using this as Dream-Poisoning? Maybe character would be stir in the sleep to kill humans, so the mortals would suspect deaths coming from the &quot;monsters&quot; that are PCs and start to hunt for them? This scenario leads even quicker to making the Freehold for protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) They go along with your plan. This actually the riskiest and most damaging course of action from a Changeling perspective. What the above posters are saying about overexposure of Gentry is true for multiple reasons. Just spending time with a True Fae long enough to have a conversation is a major Clarity breaking point. This alone should dissuade your players from sticking around to chat. Nowhere in any of the books (from what I remember) does it say anything about Exiled or Charlatan Fae being exempt from this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do not see this. I do not use classical Clarity, only house rules Dichotomy ( on which you can read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points/page4\">here</a> ). Yes, probably making things for Exiled would take you more in the way in to Dichotomy 0 point, where you are actling like a Fae - but talking to him should not. And even making his demands, at least for time, would not lead you to unplayable character territory. More fae than human, yes, but not &quot;I'm a wicked True Fae&quot;, not at least for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the group then decides to start taking orders from the thing, regardless of the motivations, every other changeling that discovers this will consider them Loyalists. The fact that it's to save some lives will be irrelevant: many Loyalists work for their masters with similar threats or incentives looming over them. &quot;Bring me pretty things or your family spends a season on the Hurting-Go-Round...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, I will have inner spies in the Freehold from the start - when other players will come to play, they will not suspect 5 changelings are working for &quot;enemy&quot;. And in the end. those Loyalists are working for the good work of stopping The Game of Old Gods that plan to slaughter all changelings in few months. Saying it's grey morally area is understatement - but think what a great plot twist it is!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From your players perspective, they will resent the task given to them. Rather than curiosity pushing them to solve the case, they will try to solve the problem of &quot;How do we escape this servitude we've been forced into?&quot; They'll keep looking for the opportunity to enact any of the other options above, probably after freeing the hostages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, more ideas for interesting scenes and plots of PCs running from abuse of Exiled intertwined with uncovering the Game of true enemies of Freehold. Once again, how it is a bad thing for the story to be told?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, all of the above is hypothetical. I hope it demonstrates all the directions a group of players can go, assuming they even accept the invitation and go to the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thank you for that, you show I could make a plot more wicked in every way they enact this plot in motion. Thanks for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely, plan a masquerade ball if that's what you want to do. Myself, I'd make the host an Ensorcelled mortal who moved to the area from another Freehold. He/she can use the opportunity to introduce the players to standard Freehold concepts: if the group has truly never meet any othe changelings outside of Arcadia, these are things they'll need to learn: the role of Courts, leadership, the threats that face the Lost and how to survive amongst regular people without turning into monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of things I want to leave on Easter game session, where PCs will form proper Freehold and choose Monarchs. This plot need to build main chronicle plot, and I see mine idea can make this - thanks once more for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder?p=377387#post377387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, yes, plant a seed for a greater plot. Have a murder but keep it a mystery. Have a bloody, exhausted Changeling drop through a bathroom mirror, having just escaped Faerie. Don't stick a fully grown tree in front of the players and say &quot;This what you're going to climb.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time I would agree with you. But I think players need to see, at least once in a chronicle, real wickedness of True Fae. And I think this &quot;You will help me, or I will kill people&quot; plan is great for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-25-2015, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}